+/**
+ * How long an anti-hang guard waits before failing the test.
+ *
+ * This is not a latency assertion — the real checks run on the rejection it
+ * returns, and a call that resolves instead of rejecting is caught by those
+ * checks whatever this value is. It only has to sit above what a helper spawn and
+ * a couple of messages cost on a loaded machine.
+ *
+ * It does NOT promise that a creation-internal error surfaces first. On the
+ * readiness path the primary error reaches the caller only after `shutdownHelper`,
+ * so the true worst case is readiness 10 s plus shutdown 5 s + 2 s — about 17 s —
+ * and this guard reports the hang before that. Neither guarded test takes that
+ * path (a missing binary is ENOENT immediately, and the fake helper announces
+ * readiness on its first line), and the same was true of the 1 s and 2 s values
+ * this replaced; it is stated so the next reader does not infer a guarantee.
+ */
+const REJECTION_GUARD_MS = 8_000;
+
